            <!-- Mathematical Formulation -->
            <div class="content-section">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div class="section-icon">🔢</div>
                    <div class="section-title">Transport Equation</div>
                </div>

                <div class="equation-box">
                    <div class="equation-title">Modified Turbulent Viscosity (ν̃)</div>
                    <div>$$\frac{\partial \tilde{\nu}}{\partial t} + u_j \frac{\partial \tilde{\nu}}{\partial x_j} = c_{b1} \tilde{S} \tilde{\nu}$$</div>
                    <div>$$- \left[c_{w1} f_w - \frac{c_{b1}}{\kappa^2} f_{t2}\right] \left(\frac{\tilde{\nu}}{d}\right)^2 + \frac{1}{\sigma}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_j}\left[(\nu + \tilde{\nu}) \frac{\partial \tilde{\nu}}{\partial x_j}\right] + \frac{c_{b2}}{\sigma}\left(\frac{\partial \tilde{\nu}}{\partial x_j}\right)^2$$</div>
                    <p style="margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #64748b;">
                        Single transport equation for modified turbulent viscosity
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="equation-box">
                    <div class="equation-title">Turbulent Viscosity</div>
                    <div>$$\nu_t = \tilde{\nu} f_{v1}, \quad f_{v1} = \frac{\chi^3}{\chi^3 + c_{v1}^3}, \quad \chi = \frac{\tilde{\nu}}{\nu}$$</div>
                    <p style="margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #64748b;">
                        Damping function ensures proper near-wall behavior
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Engineering Analogy -->
            <div class="content-section">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div class="section-icon">🧠</div>
                    <div class="section-title">Engineering Analogy</div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    <h4>🎯 Specialized Tool</h4>
                    <p><strong>Spalart-Allmaras is like a specialized aerospace tool:</strong></p>
                    <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem; padding-left: 1rem;">
                        <li><strong>Single purpose:</strong> "Designed specifically for aircraft and missiles"</li>
                        <li><strong>Simple design:</strong> "One equation instead of two - easier to implement"</li>
                        <li><strong>Proven track record:</strong> "Trusted by aerospace industry for decades"</li>
                        <li><strong>Limited scope:</strong> "Works great for its intended purpose, not general-purpose"</li>
                        <li><strong>Being replaced:</strong> "Newer tools (k-ω SST) are more versatile and accurate"</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

